BT /F1 18 Tf 72 720 Td (Chapter 1 Determinants) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 680 Td (The determinant of a matrix is a scalar value computed from its elements.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 650 Td (Definition: the determinant of an n by n matrix A is defined by the Leibniz formula.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 72 610 Td (det A = sum over permutations sign\(p\) times product of a i p\(i\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 570 Td (Motivation: determinants tell us when a system of linear equations has a unique solution.) Tj ET
endstream
